WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.641 --> 00:00:17.144
go!" Perda shouted as Trof yanked Anso's arm.

2
00:00:17.164 --> 00:00:19.566
"Don't tell me what to do!"

3
00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.327
The plonk farmer sneered.

4
00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.710
He grabbed Mellis with his free hand and glared at her.

5
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:27.993
"Did you bring your friends in to do your work for you?"

6
00:00:28.013 --> 00:00:30.154
"No, of course not!"

7
00:00:30.775 --> 00:00:31.936
Mellis cried in terror.

8
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.921
Trof narrowed his eyes.

9
00:00:33.941 --> 00:00:39.303
"Zira warned that I'd have to keep an eye on you to make sure you were working hard

10
00:00:39.343 --> 00:00:42.225
enough. It seems she was right.

11
00:00:42.825 --> 00:00:45.826
You're the laziest and sneakiest worker I've ever had!

12
00:00:46.727 --> 00:00:48.568
You're lucky I don't feed you to the plonks."

13
00:00:50.188 --> 00:00:51.469
Perda gritted her teeth.

14
00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:54.050
"What do I do now?"

15
00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.051
she thought.

16
00:00:55.071 --> 00:00:58.744
"I can zap out of here anytime.

17
00:00:58.784 --> 00:01:02.467
But I can't leave Mellis and Anso in the hands of this brute."

18
00:01:03.287 --> 00:01:05.829
She was tempted to send a Blast spell at the farmer.

19
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:07.330
But she held back.

20
00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:12.914
For one thing, it would be difficult to create enough friction for that kind of spell while shackled.

21
00:01:13.735 --> 00:01:18.518
Besides, it wouldn't be right to hurt him, even though he was holding her friends as prisoners.

22
00:01:19.119 --> 00:01:21.020
There had to be another way to save them.

23
00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.383
"Please, sir, listen to me," Perda said.

24
00:01:24.403 --> 00:01:28.573
"If you let us go, I can teach you how to use magic."

25
00:01:29.474 --> 00:01:31.475
Trof laughed.

26
00:01:31.976 --> 00:01:37.059
"What could a child like you possibly teach an adult like me?"

27
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:42.063
"I may be young, but I've been doing magic my whole life," Perda replied.

28
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:45.545
"I come from a world where magic has existed forever.

29
00:01:46.246 --> 00:01:51.089
And the magic here in Terrica seems to work the same way as it does in my world."

30
00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:53.591
"Another world?"

31
00:01:54.111 --> 00:01:55.252
The man looked skeptical.

32
00:01:55.808 --> 00:01:58.369
"That's a very creative story, young lady.

33
00:01:58.929 --> 00:02:00.790
But don't expect me to believe it!"

34
00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.810
"I can't prove that I'm from a different world.

35
00:02:04.391 --> 00:02:06.131
But I'll prove I can do magic.

36
00:02:06.611 --> 00:02:12.393
Watch!" Perda snapped her fingers a couple of times, since she couldn't rub her hands together while shackled.

37
00:02:13.013 --> 00:02:14.934
A piece of fruit appeared in her hand.

38
00:02:14.954 --> 00:02:19.675
"See?" Trof looked surprised, and then suspicious.

39
00:02:19.695 --> 00:02:21.936
"Where did that come from?"

40
00:02:22.296 --> 00:02:22.756
he asked.

41
00:02:23.484 --> 00:02:26.887
"I was told that only certain people can perform magic.

42
00:02:27.507 --> 00:02:31.350
You must have had that fruit hidden in your clothes or something."

43
00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:34.432
"No, I created it with magic."

44
00:02:35.012 --> 00:02:36.813
Perda tossed the fruit to the plonks.

45
00:02:37.674 --> 00:02:40.876
A large one grabbed it and gobbled it up, snorting happily.

46
00:02:41.397 --> 00:02:43.398
The other plonks squealed hungrily.

47
00:02:43.418 --> 00:02:46.840
"I can teach you how to do it too," Perda said.

48
00:02:47.481 --> 00:02:52.852
She quickly created more food, making sure there was enough for all the plonks.

49
00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:56.453
Soon the creatures were chomping, chewing, and grunting with joy.

50
00:02:57.453 --> 00:02:58.834
Trof's eyes narrowed.

51
00:02:58.854 --> 00:03:01.115
"Are you trying to trick me?

52
00:03:01.795 --> 00:03:07.616
If you truly can create something out of nothing, why not create something more useful?

53
00:03:08.197 --> 00:03:12.758
Perhaps a new board to replace the one the plonks broke yesterday?"

54
00:03:13.498 --> 00:03:16.459
He gestured to a cracked section of the rickety wooden fence.

55
00:03:16.479 --> 00:03:19.360
"Sure, I can do that," Perda said.

56
00:03:20.092 --> 00:03:24.514
She created more friction, and moments later a board appeared in front of Trof.

57
00:03:25.254 --> 00:03:26.415
His eyes widened.

58
00:03:26.435 --> 00:03:29.056
"You did that by snapping your fingers?"

59
00:03:29.076 --> 00:03:31.037
"Basically, yes."

60
00:03:31.877 --> 00:03:34.118
Perda briefly explained how friction worked.

61
00:03:34.138 --> 00:03:36.499
"Go ahead and try it," she said.

62
00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:43.362
"You can create anything you need—more boards, nails, food anything except humans or animals."

63
00:03:44.262 --> 00:03:46.123
Trof still looked suspicious.

64
00:03:46.643 --> 00:03:50.525
But he dropped his hold on Anso, who sidled a short distance away.

65
00:03:51.166 --> 00:03:52.107
Trof didn't notice.

66
00:03:52.647 --> 00:03:54.148
He was busy snapping his fingers.

67
00:03:54.168 --> 00:03:56.290
"Nails!" he shouted.

68
00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.272
Several nails appeared in his hand.

69
00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:00.653
He gasped.

70
00:04:00.993 --> 00:04:01.974
"It worked!

71
00:04:02.654 --> 00:04:04.155
I did magic!"

72
00:04:04.816 --> 00:04:06.157
Perda smiled and nodded.

73
00:04:06.817 --> 00:04:09.039
She wished that Trof would let go of Mellis.

74
00:04:09.739 --> 00:04:12.921
Then she could grab her and Anso and zap them all away.

75
00:04:13.582 --> 00:04:18.741
But the farmer was keeping a tight hold on Mellis' arm, even as he continued snapping with the

76
00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:19.261
other hand.

77
00:04:19.861 --> 00:04:24.303
He went on to create a new hat for himself, a hammer to help him fix the fence,

78
00:04:24.683 --> 00:04:25.884
and several more boards.

79
00:04:25.904 --> 00:04:27.565
"But wait!"

80
00:04:27.965 --> 00:04:30.086
he exclaimed as a board dropped at his feet.

81
00:04:30.106 --> 00:04:34.187
"Why should I waste my time building the fence myself?

82
00:04:34.888 --> 00:04:36.468
Can I make one by magic?"

83
00:04:37.129 --> 00:04:40.390
Perda shrugged, still trying to figure out how they could all escape.

84
00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.391
"Sure," she said.

85
00:04:42.411 --> 00:04:45.272
"You'll need a little more friction for that though.

86
00:04:45.884 --> 00:04:48.325
You could try rubbing both your hands together."

87
00:04:49.166 --> 00:04:51.787
She hoped that would make him drop his hold on Mellis.

88
00:04:52.768 --> 00:04:56.270
Instead he rubbed his free hand vigorously against his belly.

89
00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:57.951
"New fence!"

90
00:04:58.471 --> 00:04:58.871
he cried.

91
00:04:58.891 --> 00:05:01.893
"Tall and strong, so the plonks can't break out!"

92
00:05:02.693 --> 00:05:05.755
A tall, sturdy fence appeared around the plonk pen.

93
00:05:05.775 --> 00:05:07.516
"Very nice."

94
00:05:08.296 --> 00:05:10.558
Perda was still trying to come up with a plan.

95
00:05:10.578 --> 00:05:14.720
"Er, did you say your worker is sneaky?

96
00:05:15.564 --> 00:05:17.686
I can show you how to control her better.

97
00:05:17.706 --> 00:05:20.128
I'll demonstrate on this boy."

98
00:05:21.109 --> 00:05:22.270
She pointed at Anso.

99
00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:26.974
"Shackle!" Loose shackles appeared on Anso's wrists.

100
00:05:27.715 --> 00:05:29.016
"Hey!" he cried.

101
00:05:29.576 --> 00:05:30.757
Trof's eyes lit up.

102
00:05:30.777 --> 00:05:35.061
"I bet I can do that," he said, turning to Mellis.

103
00:05:35.962 --> 00:05:37.123
Perda's heart sank.

104
00:05:37.743 --> 00:05:42.267
She'd planned to offer to shackle Mellis' arms as well, so that Trof would let go of her.

105
00:05:43.148 --> 00:05:48.252
Then Perda could zap the three of them away and release Anso and Mellis from their shackles once

106
00:05:48.292 --> 00:05:48.872
they'd landed.

107
00:05:49.633 --> 00:05:54.236
But if Trof was the one to put a Shackle spell on Mellis, only he could undo it.

108
00:05:54.996 --> 00:05:57.558
The man was already rubbing his hand on his belly again.

109
00:05:57.578 --> 00:06:00.781
"All right, what was the word you used again?"

110
00:06:01.181 --> 00:06:01.681
he asked.

111
00:06:02.422 --> 00:06:07.085
Before Perda could figure out how to respond, there was a loud whistle from overhead.

112
00:06:07.706 --> 00:06:10.608
A second later the new fence burst into flames.

113
00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:14.163
Startled, the plonks ran all around, squealing.

114
00:06:14.804 --> 00:06:19.849
Trof cried out in surprise and fear, and Mellis and Anso both looked scared.

115
00:06:20.509 --> 00:06:26.135
But Perda felt a flash of hope when she looked up and saw a little, red dragon dive-bombing

116
00:06:26.175 --> 00:06:27.396
another section of fence.

117
00:06:28.457 --> 00:06:30.039
"Zing!" she cried.
